@startuml direct-rialto-handshake-cancel-supersede-sequence
title Handshake: Rialto cancels or replaces an open needData request
skinparam shadowing false

participant "Rialto event thread" as EV
participant "AampRialtoMediaSource" as SRC
participant "NeedDataHandshake" as HS
participant "Injector thread" as INJ
participant "IMediaPipeline" as PIPE

note over EV, PIPE
  direct-rialto has no needData timer of its own.  A request that
  Rialto no longer wants arrives as cancelNeedMediaData, or is
  implicitly replaced by a newer needData.
end note

== Rialto cancels request 7 ==
EV -> SRC : handleCancelNeedData()
SRC -> HS : OnCancelNeedData()
note right of HS
  hasPending = false, batch cleared, cv.notify_all().
  No haveData is sent (Rialto cancelled it).
end note
alt injector is waiting in WaitForRequest
  HS -> INJ : wakes, predicate false, keeps waiting for the next needData
else injector already holding req 7 (between WaitForRequest and Complete)
  INJ -> PIPE : addSegment(7, segment)
  PIPE --> INJ : status (stale request id)
  INJ -> HS : Complete(gen, 7, ...)
  HS --> INJ : Reply::None (request no longer owned)
  note right of INJ
    The sample counts as consumed.  Only NO_SPACE keeps a sample
    for retry; an addSegment error is logged and the sample dropped.
  end note
end

== Rialto issues needData 8 while 7 is still unanswered ==
EV -> SRC : handleNeedData(N, req=8)
SRC -> HS : OnNeedData(N, 8)
HS --> SRC : superseded = Claim(7), request 8 staged
SRC -> PIPE : haveData(NO_AVAILABLE_SAMPLES, 7)
@enduml
